1
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,480
太上老君说常清静妙经
The Wondrous Scripture of Constant Clarity and Stillness, Spoken by the Most High Lord Lao

2
00:00:31,699 --> 00:00:33,402
老君曰：
Lord Lao said:

3
00:00:33,623 --> 00:00:36,814
大道无形，生育天地；
The Great Dao has no form, yet gives birth to Heaven and Earth.

4
00:00:37,036 --> 00:00:40,108
大道无情，运行日月；
The Great Dao has no feeling, yet moves the sun and moon.

5
00:00:40,326 --> 00:00:43,399
大道无名，长养万物。
The Great Dao has no name, yet nurtures all things.

6
00:00:43,618 --> 00:00:47,003
吾不知其名，强名曰道。
I do not know its name; compelled to name it, I call it Dao.

7
00:00:47,222 --> 00:00:51,399
夫道者，有清有浊，有动有静。
Within the Dao are clarity and turbidity, movement and stillness.

8
00:00:51,618 --> 00:00:55,027
天清地浊，天动地静，
Heaven is clear; Earth is turbid. Heaven moves; Earth is still.

9
00:00:55,246 --> 00:00:58,584
男清女浊，男动女静。
The male is clear; the female is turbid. The male moves; the female is still.

10
00:00:58,804 --> 00:01:01,899
降本流末，而生万物。
Descending from the root and flowing to the branches, they give birth to all things.

11
00:01:02,118 --> 00:01:05,768
清者浊之源，动者静之基。
Clarity is the source of turbidity; movement is the foundation of stillness.

12
00:01:05,986 --> 00:01:09,730
人能常清静，天地悉皆归。
If one can remain clear and still, Heaven and Earth will both return.

13
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:13,384
夫人神好清而心扰之，
The human spirit favors clarity, but the heart disturbs it.

14
00:01:13,603 --> 00:01:16,772
人心好静而欲牵之。
The human heart favors stillness, but desire pulls it away.

15
00:01:16,992 --> 00:01:19,992
常能遣其欲而心自静，
By continually dispelling desire, the heart becomes still of itself.

16
00:01:20,212 --> 00:01:23,043
澄其心而神自清，
By settling the heart, the spirit becomes clear of itself.

17
00:01:23,263 --> 00:01:26,792
自然六欲不生，三毒消灭。
Naturally, the six desires cease to arise, and the three poisons disappear.

18
00:01:27,012 --> 00:01:31,427
所以不能者，为心未澄、欲未遣也。
Those unable to do this have not yet settled the heart or dispelled desire.

19
00:01:31,647 --> 00:01:36,183
能遣之者，内观於心，心无其心；
Those who can dispel desire look inward at the heart: the heart is without a heart.

20
00:01:36,403 --> 00:01:39,956
外观於形，形无其形；
They look outward at form: form is without a form.

21
00:01:40,176 --> 00:01:43,462
远观於物，物无其物。
They look afar at things: things are without their thingness.

22
00:01:43,683 --> 00:01:46,852
三者既悟，唯见於空。
Once these three are understood, only emptiness is seen.

23
00:01:47,072 --> 00:01:50,263
观空亦空，空无所空。
Contemplating emptiness, emptiness too is empty; emptiness has nothing to empty.

24
00:01:50,483 --> 00:01:53,652
所空既无，无无亦无。
With nothing left to empty, even the absence of absence is absent.

25
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:56,992
无无既无，湛然常寂。
When even the absence of absence is gone, there is profound, constant serenity.

26
00:01:57,212 --> 00:02:00,427
寂无所寂，欲岂能生？
With nothing left to make serene, how could desire arise?

27
00:02:00,647 --> 00:02:03,718
欲既不生，即是真静。
When desire no longer arises, this is true stillness.

28
00:02:03,938 --> 00:02:07,132
真常应物，真常得性。
In true constancy, respond to things; in true constancy, realize your nature.

29
00:02:07,352 --> 00:02:10,831
常应常静，常清净矣。
Always responding, always still: thus one is always clear and pure.

30
00:02:11,052 --> 00:02:14,170
如此清静，渐入真道。
Through such clarity and stillness, one gradually enters the true Dao.

31
00:02:14,391 --> 00:02:17,367
既入真道，名为得道。
Having entered the true Dao, one is said to have attained the Dao.

32
00:02:17,586 --> 00:02:20,780
虽名得道，实无所得。
Though called attaining the Dao, in truth nothing is attained.

33
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
为化众生，名为得道。
To transform sentient beings, it is called attaining the Dao.

34
00:02:24,218 --> 00:02:27,268
能悟之者，可传圣道。
Those who can awaken to this may transmit the sacred Dao.

35
00:02:27,486 --> 00:02:29,192
老君曰：
Lord Lao said:

36
00:02:29,412 --> 00:02:32,604
上士无争，下士好争；
Superior adepts do not contend; inferior adepts delight in contention.

37
00:02:32,824 --> 00:02:35,919
上德不德，下德执德。
Higher virtue does not regard itself as virtuous; lower virtue clings to virtue.

38
00:02:36,139 --> 00:02:39,211
执着之者，不名道德。
Those who cling cannot be said to possess the Dao and its virtue.

39
00:02:39,431 --> 00:02:43,318
众生所以不得真道者，为有妄心。
Sentient beings fail to attain the true Dao because they have deluded hearts.

40
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:46,828
既有妄心，即惊其神。
Once the heart is deluded, the spirit is disturbed.

41
00:02:47,048 --> 00:02:50,336
既惊其神，即着万物。
Once the spirit is disturbed, it becomes attached to all things.

42
00:02:50,556 --> 00:02:53,818
既着万物，即生贪求。
Once attached to all things, craving and grasping arise.

43
00:02:54,038 --> 00:02:57,256
既生贪求，即是烦恼。
Once craving and grasping arise, there is affliction.

44
00:02:57,474 --> 00:03:00,812
烦恼妄想，忧苦身心，
Affliction and deluded thoughts bring sorrow and suffering to body and heart.

45
00:03:01,032 --> 00:03:04,223
便遭浊辱，流浪生死，
Thus one suffers defilement and disgrace, wandering through birth and death.

46
00:03:04,443 --> 00:03:07,804
常沉苦海，永失真道。
Forever sinking in the sea of suffering, one loses the true Dao.

47
00:03:08,024 --> 00:03:11,048
真常之道，悟者自得。
The Dao of true constancy is attained by those who awaken to it themselves.

48
00:03:11,268 --> 00:03:14,340
得悟道者，常清静矣。
Those who awaken to the Dao are always clear and still.

49
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:17,008
仙人葛仙翁曰：
The immortal Elder Ge said:

50
00:03:17,228 --> 00:03:20,828
吾得真道，曾诵此经万遍。
I attained the true Dao, having recited this scripture ten thousand times.

51
00:03:21,048 --> 00:03:24,936
此经是天人所习，不传下士。
This scripture is studied by celestial beings and is not transmitted to inferior adepts.

52
00:03:25,156 --> 00:03:28,180
吾昔受之於东华帝君，
Long ago, I received it from the Sovereign Lord of Eastern Florescence.

53
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:32,072
东华帝君受之於金阙帝君，
The Lord of Eastern Florescence received it from the Lord of the Golden Palace.

54
00:03:32,292 --> 00:03:35,818
金阙帝君受之於西王母，
The Sovereign Lord of the Golden Palace received it from the Queen Mother of the West.

55
00:03:36,038 --> 00:03:40,216
西王母皆口口相传，不记文字。
From the Queen Mother of the West, it was passed from mouth to mouth, never recorded in writing.

56
00:03:40,436 --> 00:03:43,842
吾今於世，书而录之。
Now, in this world, I write it down and record it.

57
00:03:44,062 --> 00:03:47,568
上士悟之，升为天官；
Superior adepts awaken to it and ascend to become celestial officials.

58
00:03:47,788 --> 00:03:51,122
中士得之，南官列仙；
Middle adepts attain it and join the ranks of immortals in the Southern Offices.

59
00:03:51,342 --> 00:03:54,608
下士修之，在世长年。
Inferior adepts practice it and enjoy long years in this world.

60
00:03:54,828 --> 00:03:58,306
游行三界，升入金门。
They roam the Three Realms and ascend through the Golden Gate.

61
00:03:58,526 --> 00:04:00,711
左玄真人曰：
The Perfected One Zuoxuan said:

62
00:04:00,931 --> 00:04:04,436
学道之士，持诵此经者，
Students of the Dao who uphold and recite this scripture

63
00:04:04,656 --> 00:04:07,991
即得十天善神拥护其人，
receive the protection of the benevolent spirits of the Ten Heavens.

64
00:04:08,211 --> 00:04:11,740
然后玉符保神，金液炼形，
Then jade talismans safeguard the spirit, and golden fluid refines the body.

65
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:15,080
形神俱妙，与道合真。
Body and spirit both become wondrous, united with the Dao in perfection.

66
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:17,388
正一真人曰：
The Perfected One Zhengyi said:

67
00:04:17,608 --> 00:04:21,038
人家有此经，悟解之者，
When a household possesses this scripture, those who awaken to its meaning

68
00:04:21,259 --> 00:04:24,379
灾障不干，众圣护门，
are untouched by calamities and hindrances; the holy ones guard their gates.

69
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:27,983
神升上界，朝拜高尊。
Their spirits ascend to the upper realms to pay homage to the exalted ones.

70
00:04:28,204 --> 00:04:31,444
功满德就，相感帝君。
With merit and virtue fulfilled, they resonate with the Sovereign Lord.

71
00:04:31,663 --> 00:04:35,048
诵持不退，身腾紫云。
Unwavering in recitation and observance, they rise bodily upon purple clouds.
